Troubleshooting Tips
Common Issues and Solutions
Issue: Pods stuck in Pending state

# Check node resources
kubectl describe nodes

# Check pod events
kubectl describe pod <pod-name>
Issue: Argo CD UI not accessible

# Check if port-forward is running
ps aux | grep port-forward

# Restart port-forward if needed
pkill -f "port-forward"
kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8080:443 --address=0.0.0.0 &
Issue: Application sync fails

# Check application events
argocd app get sample-app --output yaml

# Check Kubernetes events
kubectl get events --sort-by=.metadata.creationTimestamp
Issue: CLI authentication problems

# Re-login to Argo CD
argocd logout
argocd login localhost:8080 --username admin --insecure
Key Concepts Learned
Argo CD Architecture Components
API Server: Exposes the API consumed by Web UI, CLI, and CI/CD systems
Repository Server: Internal service that maintains a local cache of Git repositories
Application Controller: Kubernetes controller that continuously monitors running applications
Redis: Used for caching and as a message broker
Dex: Identity service for authentication (optional)
GitOps Principles
Declarative: System state is described declaratively
Versioned: Configuration is stored in Git with full version history
Automated: Changes are automatically applied to the system
Monitored: System continuously monitors and corrects drift
Argo CD Key Features
Application Management: Deploy and manage applications across multiple environments
Git Integration: Sync applications from Git repositories automatically
Multi-tenancy: Support for multiple projects and RBAC
Health Monitoring: Continuous monitoring of application health
Rollback Capabilities: Easy rollback to previous application states
